adjudication.rationale:
In the newly added API route `apps/web/pages/api/webhook/app-credential.ts`, the webhook authentication check directly compares a request header to `process.env.CALCOM_WEBHOOK_SECRET` using `!==`:

```ts
if (
  req.headers[process.env.CALCOM_WEBHOOK_HEADER_NAME || "calcom-webhook-secret"] !==
  process.env.CALCOM_WEBHOOK_SECRET
) {
  return res.status(403).json({ message: "Invalid webhook secret" });
}
```

This is a normal JavaScript string/primitive comparison and is not constant-time. Since this value is being used as an authenticator (“webhook secret”), this introduces a timing side-channel risk (the comparison can exit early), so the finding describes a real security issue present in the diff.
